file handling:
--> in shell scripting reading from a file means taking data from a file and using it in the script.
--> writing data to a file means storing output/data in a file.

*writing to a file:
1. > = create/overwrite a file
---> if file does not exist, it is created. and if it already exists, its old content is overwritten

2. >> = append to a file
--> this adds the text at the end of the file.
